the boost that is embedded in rstan. This might enable us to get rstan onto
CRAN if we split it into two packages.

But after loading the rstan package, I wasn't able to compile an example
Bayesian model with BH. I think this is only due to not having

functional.hpp

in the include/boost directory of the BH package. The functional/
subdirectory is there so omitting functional.hpp may be a bug.

There are a couple of other hurdles, but I think those are on our end.

Thanks,
Ben
